# NYC 311 Service Requests Analysis

## Project Goal

The goal of this project is to analyze NYC 311 service requests and investigate how service request resolution times vary across different complaint types and boroughs.

## Research Question

How does the resolution time of NYC 311 service requests vary across different complaint types and NYC boroughs?

## Data Source

I will use the NYC 311 Service Requests dataset, which contains information about service requests made by residents and visitors in New York City. The dataset includes information such as complaint type, borough, creation date, and closing date.

## Analysis Approach

First, I will clean and prepare the data using Python and Pandas. I will calculate the resolution time for each service request using the creation and closing dates.

I will then compare the average and distribution of resolution times across different NYC boroughs and complaint types. I will also identify which complaint types occur most frequently in each borough.

I plan to use data visualizations such as bar charts and time-based graphs to identify patterns and differences in the data.

## Expected Results

I expect to identify differences in service request volume and resolution times between boroughs and complaint types. The analysis may help show which types of service requests take longer to resolve and whether resolution times vary by location.

## Future Analysis

Based on the initial results, I may investigate additional factors such as time of year, day of the week, or specific complaint categories to better understand the patterns in NYC 311 service requests.
